==Swedish==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|sv|/²ɡɑːlɛn/}}
* {{audio|sv|Sv-galen.ogg}} {{attention|sv|not sure if pronunciation is the same for both etymologies}}

===Etymology 1===

====Participle====
{{head|sv|past participle}}

# {{past participle of|sv|gala}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|sv|gmq-osw|galin}}, from {{der|sv|non|galinn}}.

====Adjective====
{{sv-adj|galnare|galnast}}

# [[crazy]], [[insane]] (e.g. of a person or situation)
#: {{ux|sv|Han är '''galen'''|He is '''crazy'''}}
#: {{ux|sv|Han blev '''galen''' av ilska|He went '''crazy''' with anger}}
# {{lb|sv|with {{m|sv|i||in}}}} crazy about (loving)
#: {{ux|sv|Jag är '''galen i''' majs|I'm '''crazy about''' corn}}
# [[wrong]], [[amiss]]
#: {{ux|sv|Ojdå, det där blev lite '''galet'''|Oops, that turned out a bit '''crazy'''}}
# (gone) [[awry]] (not according to plan)
#: {{syn|sv|fel|snett|på tok}}
#: {{ux|sv|Det gick '''galet'''|It went '''awry''' (turned out crazy)}}

=====Usage notes=====
''Gå galet'' always means ''go awry'', rather than ''go crazy''; the latter is instead expressed as ''bli galen''.

